          simpleExplanation: '• Notations: O (Upper bound / Worst case), Omega (Lower bound / Best case), Theta (Tight bound / Average case).\n• Master Theorem: T(n) = a * T(n / b) + f(n), where a >= 1, b > 1.\n  Compute n^(log_b a) and compare with f(n) = n^k:\n  - Case 1: If log_b a > k -> T(n) = Theta(n^(log_b a)).\n  - Case 2: If log_b a == k -> T(n) = Theta(n^k * log n).\n  - Case 3: If log_b a < k -> T(n) = Theta(f(n)).',
